<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hayreddin Barbarossa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1478–<a href="/years/1546">1546</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hayreddin Barbarossa was a sixteenth-century corsair who became grand admiral of the Ottoman fleet. He secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and won a major victory over a Christian fleet at Preveza in 1538. He helped make the Ottoman Empire the dominant naval power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa.jpg" alt="Hayreddin Barbarossa" width="236" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AsiaticLion7 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hayreddin_-_Algeria_Fine_Art_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
